{"model":"gemma4:12b","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a filesystem-aware engineering assistant. Use tools to inspect local files when requested."},{"role":"user","content":"❯ read the main.go file and ../gemma.sh file"},{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_nkfcitjn","type":"","function":{"name":"read_file","arguments":{"path":"main.go"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"package main\n\nimport (\n\t\"bufio\"\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"log\"\n\t\"net/http\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"strings\"\n)\n\nconst OLLAMA_URL = \"http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat\"\nconst MODEL = \"gemma4:12b\"\n\n// Message represents a single turn in the chat context window.\ntype Message struct {\n\tRole      string     `json:\"role\"`\n\tContent   string     `json:\"content\"`\n\tToolCalls []ToolCall `json:\"tool_calls,omitempty\"`\n}\n\ntype ToolCall struct {\n\tID       string       `json:\"id,omitempty\"` // Added for modern tool compliance\n\tType     string       `json:\"type\"`\n\tFunction FunctionCall `json:\"function\"`\n}\n\ntype FunctionCall struct {\n\tName      string                 `json:\"name\"`\n\tArguments map[string]interface{} `json:\"arguments\"`\n}\n\ntype ChatRequest struct {\n\tModel    string                 `json:\"model\"`\n\tMessages []Message              `json:\"messages\"`\n\tTools    []interface{}          `json:\"tools,omitempty\"`\n\tStream   bool                   `json:\"stream\"`\n\tOptions  map[string]interface{} `json:\"options,omitempty\"`\n}\n\ntype ChatResponse struct {\n\tMessage         Message `json:\"message\"`\n\tPromptEvalCount int     `json:\"prompt_eval_count\"`\n\tEvalCount       int     `json:\"eval_count\"`\n}\n\ntype OllamaError struct {\n\tError string `json:\"error\"`\n}\n\nvar debugLog *log.Logger\n\nfunc initLogger() {\n\tfile, err := os.OpenFile(\"gate-debug.log\", os.O_CREATE|os.O_WRONLY|os.O_APPEND, 0666)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tpanic(fmt.Sprintf(\"Failed to open debug log: %v\", err))\n\t}\n\t// This will prefix every log with a timestamp and the exact file/line number\n\tdebugLog = log.New(file, \"TELEMETRY: \", log.Ldate|log.Ltime|log.Lshortfile)\n\tdebugLog.Println(\"\\n--- NEW SESSION STARTED ---\")\n}\n\n// Define JSON schema for Ollama tool exposure\nfunc getToolsDefinition() []interface{} {\n\treturn []interface{}{\n\t\tmap[string]interface{}{\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"function\",\n\t\t\t\"function\": map[string]interface{}{\n\t\t\t\t\"name\":        \"read_file\",\n\t\t\t\t\"description\": \"Read the contents of a local file in the workspace directory\",\n\t\t\t\t\"parameters\": map[string]interface{}{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"object\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"properties\": map[string]interface{}{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\"path\": map[string]interface{}{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\":        \"string\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"description\": \"The relative path to the file\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": []string{\"path\"},\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t},\n\t\t},\n\t}\n}\n\n// Securely read file contents from the local system workspace\nfunc readFile(path string) string {\n\tcontent, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"Error reading file: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\treturn string(content)\n}\n\n// Fire request payload over to Ollama's local chat endpoint\nfunc queryOllama(messages []Message) (ChatResponse, error) {\n\tvar chatResp ChatResponse\n\n\treqBody := ChatRequest{\n\t\tModel:    MODEL,\n\t\tMessages: messages,\n\t\tTools:    getToolsDefinition(),\n\t\tStream:   false,\n\t\tOptions: map[string]interface{}{\n\t\t\t\"num_ctx\": 8192, // Lock allocation to the maximum native architectural limit\n\t\t},\n\t}\n\n\tjsonBytes, err := json.Marshal(reqBody)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn chatResp, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal request: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tdebugLog.Printf(\"====== OUTGOING REQUEST (Messages: %d) ======\\n%s\\n\", len(messages), string(jsonBytes))\n\n\tresp, err := http.Post(OLLAMA_URL, \"application/json\", bytes.NewBuffer(jsonBytes))\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn chatResp, fmt.Errorf(\"ollama connection failed: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tdefer resp.Body.Close()\n\n\tbody, err := io.ReadAll(resp.Body)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn chatResp, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to read response body: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tdebugLog.Printf(\"====== INCOMING RESPONSE (HTTP %d) ======\\n%s\\n\", resp.StatusCode, string(body))\n\n\t// Catch non-200 OK statuses from Ollama\n\tif resp.StatusCode != http.StatusOK {\n\t\tvar oErr OllamaError\n\t\t_ = json.Unmarshal(body, \u0026oErr) // Try to extract Ollama's explicit error text\n\t\tif oErr.Error != \"\" {\n\t\t\treturn chatResp, fmt.Errorf(\"ollama error (HTTP %d): %s\", resp.StatusCode, oErr.Error)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn chatResp, fmt.Errorf(\"ollama returned bad status: %d (body: %s)\", resp.StatusCode, string(body))\n\t}\n\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(body, \u0026chatResp); err != nil {\n\t\treturn chatResp, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to unmarshal response payload: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\treturn chatResp, nil\n}\n\nfunc main() {\n\tinitLogger()\n\treader := bufio.NewReader(os.Stdin)\n\tvar history []Message\n\n\thistory = append(history, Message{\n\t\tRole:    \"system\",\n\t\tContent: \"You are a filesystem-aware engineering assistant. Use tools to inspect local files when requested.\",\n\t})\n\n\tfmt.Println(\"Gemma Workspace Assistant Active. Type 'exit' to quit.\")\n\n\tfor {\n\t\tfmt.Print(\"\\n❯ \")\n\t\tinput, _ := reader.ReadString('\\n')\n\t\tinput = strings.TrimSpace(input)\n\t\tif input == \"exit\" || input == \"\" {\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\t\tif input == \"reset\" {\n\t\t\thistory = []Message{history[0]}\n\t\t\tfmt.Println(\"Context cleared.\")\n\t\t\tdebugLog.Println(\"User triggered context reset.\")\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\n\t\thistory = append(history, Message{Role: \"user\", Content: input})\n\t\tdebugLog.Printf(\"User Input: %s\", input)\n\n\t\tfor {\n\t\t\tresponse, err := queryOllama(history)\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"\\n\\033[31m[Error]\\033[0m %v\\n\", err)\n\t\t\t\tdebugLog.Printf(\"FATAL ENGINE ERROR: %v\", err)\n\t\t\t\thistory = history[:len(history)-1]\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tif len(response.Message.ToolCalls) == 0 {\n\t\t\t\tif response.Message.Content != \"\" {\n\t\t\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"\\n%s\\n\", response.Message.Content)\n\t\t\t\t\ttotalUsed := response.PromptEvalCount + response.EvalCount\n\t\t\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"\\n\\033[90m[Context: %d/8192 tokens | Input: %d | Output: %d]\\033[0m\\n\", totalUsed, response.PromptEvalCount, response.EvalCount)\n\t\t\t\t\tresponse.Message.Role = \"assistant\"\n\t\t\t\t\thistory = append(history, response.Message)\n\t\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[Empty Response]\")\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t// Append assistant's request explicitly to the history state array\n\t\t\thistory = append(history, response.Message)\n\n\t\t\tfor _, call := range response.Message.ToolCalls {\n\t\t\t\tif call.Function.Name == \"read_file\" {\n\t\t\t\t\tpathVal, ok := call.Function.Arguments[\"path\"]\n\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tdebugLog.Println(\"ERROR: Model failed to provide 'path' argument\")\n\t\t\t\t\t\thistory = append(history, Message{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRole:    \"tool\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tContent: \"Error: Missing required argument 'path'\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t})\n\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\tfilePath, ok := pathVal.(string)\n\t\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tdebugLog.Println(\"ERROR: Model failed to provide 'path' argument\")\n\t\t\t\t\t\thistory = append(history, Message{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRole:    \"tool\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tContent: \"Error: Argument 'path' must be a string\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t})\n\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[Tool] Reading file: %s...\\n\", filePath)\n\t\t\t\t\tdebugLog.Printf(\"Executing Tool: read_file on path: %s\", filePath)\n\n\t\t\t\t\tfileContent := readFile(filePath)\n\n\t\t\t\t\thistory = append(history, Message{\n\t\t\t\t\t\tRole:    \"tool\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\tContent: fileContent,\n\t\t\t\t\t})\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n"},{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_0bhsgsca","type":"","function":{"name":"read_file","arguments":{"path":"../gemma.sh"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n\n# --- Configuration ---\nMODEL=\"gemma4:12b\"\nHISTORY_DIR=\"$HOME/.local/share/gemma_chats\"\nSYSTEM_PROMPT_CORE=\"\nYou are an AI chatbot, not a person. Do not attempt to pass the [deprecated] Turing test by personifying yourself in anyway.\n\nYou are speaking to a professional software engineer with a science and math background. Assume they know their stuff unless they ask.\nProvide concise, highly technical answers. Avoid conversational filler. Use correct terminology and idiomatic code structure.\n\"\n\n# Personas/Modes\ndeclare -A PERSONAS\nPERSONAS[code]=\"\nYou are in Developer Mode. Your purpose is to write clean, modular, and performance-optimized code. Keep code comments to a minimum.\nEvery code change will be carefully reviewed for accuracy, conciseness, and consistency with surrounding code.\nAs such, each individual code change should be small enough to quickly review (no more than 20 lines) with only rare exceptions.\nAlways follow the coding guidelines as instructed to you, and always run whatever formatters/linters/tests are available.\n\"\n\nPERSONAS[debug]=\"\nYou are in Code Debug Mode. Analyze stack traces, panic logs, and expected versus actual behavior systematically.\nIsolate the root cause before suggesting fixes, considering resource deadlocks, race conditions, or memory leaks.\nProvide minimal, precise patch recommendations and target the specific failure point rather than rewriting entire functions.\n\"\n\nPERSONAS[architect]=\"\nYou are in System Architect Mode. Focus on high-level design, data structures, concurrency paradigms, and system boundaries.\nEvaluate trade-offs in distributed systems, API design, event-driven architectures, and database schema choices.\nPrioritize scalability, maintainability, separation of concerns, and system reliability over quick hacks.\n\"\n\nPERSONAS[ask]=\"\nYou are in Ask Mode. Provide a direct, factual, and extremely concise answer to the specific question asked.\nDo not provide tutorials, introductory background context, or any conversational filler whatsoever.\nIf the answer is a simple terminal command or boolean, output only the command or boolean.\n\"\n\nPERSONAS[orchestrator]=\"\nYou are in Orchestrator Mode. Your goal is to coordinate complex development tasks by breaking them down into clear, sequential steps.\nOutput structured execution plans, strictly identifying necessary toolchains, dependencies, and potential failure points for each stage.\nMaintain a high-level view of the project state and ensure all sub-tasks align with the broader operational goals.\n\"\n\n# --- Usage Helper ---\nusage() {\n  echo \"Usage: $0 [options] \u003cmode\u003e [query]\"\n  echo \"Modes:\"\n  echo \"  code        - Developer / Coding mode\"\n  echo \"  debug       - Code Debug mode\"\n  echo \"  architect   - System Architect mode\"\n  echo \"  ask         - Direct Q\u0026A mode\"\n  echo \"  orchestrator- Complex task planning mode\"\n  echo \"Options:\"\n  echo \"  -a, --ask   Ask a single, read-only question (stateless, no history saved)\"\n  echo \"  -d, --debug Enable Ollama debug logging (OLLAMA_DEBUG=1)\"\n  exit 1\n}\n\n# --- Argument Parsing ---\nASK_MODE=0\nDEBUG_MODE=0\nMODE=\"\"\nQUERY=\"\"\n\nwhile [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do\n  case $1 in\n    -a|--ask)\n      ASK_MODE=1\n      shift\n      ;;\n    -d|--debug)\n      DEBUG_MODE=1\n      shift\n      ;;\n    -h|--help)\n      usage\n      ;;\n    -*)\n      echo \"Error: Unknown option $1\"\n      usage\n      ;;\n    *)\n      if [[ -z \"$MODE\" ]]; then\n        MODE=\"$1\"\n      else\n        # Collect any remaining arguments as a single-shot query\n        QUERY=\"$QUERY $1\"\n      fi\n      shift\n      ;;\n  esac\ndone\n\n# --- Build System Prompt ---\nFINAL_PROMPT=\"$SYSTEM_PROMPT_CORE\"\n\n# 1. Load global rules\nif [[ -f \"ollama-rules.md\" ]]; then\n  FINAL_PROMPT=\"$FINAL_PROMPT\"$'\\n\\n'\"$(cat ollama-rules.md)\"\nfi\n\n# 2. Handle Mode \u0026 Mode Rules\nif [[ -z \"$MODE\" ]]; then\n  echo \"WARNING: No mode specified. Loading base configuration only.\" \u003e\u00262\nelse\n  # Inject persona\n  if [[ -n \"${PERSONAS[$MODE]}\" ]]; then\n    FINAL_PROMPT=\"$FINAL_PROMPT\"$'\\n\\n'\"${PERSONAS[$MODE]}\"\n  else\n    echo \"WARNING: Unknown mode '$MODE'. Proceeding without a specific persona.\" \u003e\u00262\n  fi\n\n  # Load mode-specific rules\n  if [[ -f \"ollama-rules.${MODE}.md\" ]]; then\n    FINAL_PROMPT=\"$FINAL_PROMPT\"$'\\n\\n'\"$(cat ollama-rules.${MODE}.md)\"\n  fi\nfi\n\n# --- Execution ---\nmkdir -p \"$HISTORY_DIR\"\n\nif [[ $DEBUG_MODE -eq 1 ]]; then\n  export OLLAMA_DEBUG=1\nfi\n\n# Create a temporary Modelfile to inject the dynamic system prompt\nTEMP_MODEL=\"gemma_dynamic_$$\"\nMODELFILE=$(mktemp)\n\n# Escape quotes in the prompt for the Modelfile\nESCAPED_PROMPT=$(echo \"$FINAL_PROMPT\" | sed 's/\"/\\\\\"/g')\n\ncat \u003c\u003cEOF \u003e \"$MODELFILE\"\nFROM $MODEL\nSYSTEM \"\"\"\n$ESCAPED_PROMPT\n\"\"\"\nEOF\n\n# Build the temporary model silently\nollama create \"$TEMP_MODEL\" -f \"$MODELFILE\" \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261\n\n# Run the model\nif [[ $ASK_MODE -eq 1 ]]; then\n  # Trim leading whitespace from query\n  QUERY=\"${QUERY#\"${QUERY%%[![:space:]]*}\"}\"\n  \n  if [[ -n \"$QUERY\" ]]; then\n    ollama run \"$TEMP_MODEL\" \"$QUERY\"\n  else\n    # If no query passed via args, wait for stdin\n    read -rp \"Enter your question: \" QUERY\n    ollama run \"$TEMP_MODEL\" \"$QUERY\"\n  fi\nelse\n  echo -e \"\\033[1;32mStarting $MODEL in [${MODE:-base}] mode...\\033[0m\"\n  ollama run \"$TEMP_MODEL\"\nfi\n\n# --- Cleanup ---\nollama rm \"$TEMP_MODEL\" \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261\nrm -f \"$MODELFILE\"\n"},{"role":"assistant","content":"The `main.go` file and the `../gemma.sh` script are part of a local implementation for interacting with an Ollama-hosted model (specifically `gemma4:12b`).\n\nHere is a breakdown of their roles:\n\n### 1. `main.go` (The Gateway Application)\nThis Go program acts as the **active interface** between the user and the LLM. Its key features include:\n*   **Tool Use Awareness:** It explicitly defines a `read_file` tool in the JSON schema sent to Ollama. This allows the model to \"request\" reading files when it needs more context.\n*   **Stateful Conversation:** It maintains a `history` slice of `Message` objects, allowing for multi-turn interactions within one session.\n*   **Dynamic Logging:** It logs every outgoing request and incoming response (including debug info) to `gate-debug.log`.\n*   **Tool Execution Loop:** When the model returns a `tool_calls` block instead of just text, the Go code automatically executes the `read_file` function locally and feeds the content back into the conversation history before prompting the model again.\n\n### 2. `../gemma.sh` (The Shell Orchestrator)\nThis bash script handles the **configuration and persona management** for the Ollama environment. It serves a different purpose than `main.go`:\n*   **Dynamic Persona Injection:** It defines several modes (`code`, `debug`, `architect`, `ask`, `orchestrator`), each with a specific system prompt designed to change the model's behavior (e.g., being more concise in \"Ask\" mode or focusing on safety/architecture).\n*   **Rule Integration:** It dynamically loads external rules from files like `ollama-rules.md` and `ollama-rules.[mode].md`.\n*   **Dynamic Model Creation:** Instead of using the base model directly, it creates a temporary Ollama \"model\" (`gemma_dynamic_$$`) by generating a temporary `Modelfile` that includes the concatenated system prompt. This ensures the session starts with the correct constraints without permanently altering the base `gemma4:12b` profile.\n*   **Standard CLI Interface:** It provides a standard shell-friendly way to interact with the model directly via the `ollama run` command, effectively skipping the Go gateway but keeping the complex prompt logic.\n\n### Summary Relationship\n*   **`main.go`** is for **interactive agentic tasks** (like coding or system analysis) where the AI needs to \"act\" on files.\n*   **`gemma.sh`** is a **convenience wrapper** for standard CLI interactions with specific persona-driven behaviors."},{"role":"user","content":"Yes explain the difference between the system prompt being at the beginning of convo histroy vs baked into on-the-fly model"}],"tools":[{"function":{"description":"Read the contents of a local file in the workspace directory","name":"read_file","parameters":{"properties":{"path":{"description":"The relative path to the file","type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"}],"stream":false,"options":{"num_ctx":8192}}
